sentences.t:
Sessaenta e çinco cavalleros acreçídol han,
e él se tenié çiento que aduxiera d'allá;
por ir con estas dueñas buena conpaña se faze.

sentences.l:
Sixty and five knights increased-him have,
and he himself had a-hundred that he-had-brought from-there;
for to-go with these ladies good company itself makes.

sentences.t:
Quando estas dueñas adobadas las ha,
el bueno de Minaya pienssa de cavalgar;
afevos Raquel e Vidas a los pie[de]s le caen;

sentences.l:
When these ladies equipped them he-has,
the good-one of Minaya thinks of to-ride;
behold-you Raquel and Vidas at the fee[t] to-him they-fall;

sentences.t:
“Merçed, Minaya, cavallero de prestar!
Desfechos nos ha el Çid, sabet, si no nos val;
soltariemos la ganançia, que nos diesse el cabdal.”

sentences.l:
“Mercy, Minaya, knight of worth!
Undone us has the Çid, know-ye, if not us he-helps;
we-would-release the gain, provided to-us he-gave the capital.”

sentences.t:
Respuso Minaya: “fer lo he de veluntad.”
Yas espiden e pienssan de cavalgar,
el portero con ellos que los ha de aguardar;

sentences.l:
Answered Minaya: “do it I-have of will.”
Now-themselves they-take-leave and think of to-ride,
the porter with them who them has to guard;

sentences.t:
por la tierra del rey mucho conducho les dan.
De San Pero fasta Medina en çinco días van;
felos en Medina las dueñas e Álbar Fáñez.

sentences.l:
through the land of-the king much provision to-them they-give.
From San Pero as-far-as Medina in five days they-go;
behold-them in Medina the ladies and Álbar Fáñez.
